@sfofgalaxy after selecting the azure and filling the model, api_key.. was the `.env` successfully generated with your inputted data?
Yes, it has been generated.
I tried to explicitly set the `llm` parameter in my agents, it ran smoothly.
By the way, I used this crew initialization process:

llm = LLM(
    model="azure/gpt-4o"
)

    @agent
    def manager(self) -> Agent:
        return Agent(config=self.agents_config["manager"], verbose=True, llm=llm)

    @agent
    def analysis_dept(self) -> Agent:
        return Agent(
            config=self.agents_config["analysis_dept"],
            verbose=True,
            llm=llm
        )

    @crew
    def crew(self) -> Crew:
        return Crew(
            agents=[self.analysis_dept(), self.reporting_dept()],
            tasks=[self.draft_report()],
            process=Process.hierarchical, 
            manager_agent=self.manager(), 
            verbose=True
        )

but if I set `planning` to be `True`, it happened again. i.e.,

    @crew
    def crew(self) -> Crew:
        return Crew(
            agents=[self.analysis_dept(), self.reporting_dept()],
            tasks=[self.draft_report()],
            process=Process.hierarchical, 
            manager_agent=self.manager(), 
            verbose=True,
            planning=True
        )
I tried to explicitly add `planning_llm=llm` in Crew, it worked.
But I thought the `planning` capability is default for manager in hierarchical process.
May I ask if the process is hierarchical, still need set `planning`?
Because in the documentation, it says manager has the capability, I think documentation does emphasis whether should I set `planning` parameter, I didn't see it.
I found the root cause.

Ridiculously, I use `crewai create crew latest-ai-development` and the default `.env` file use `model=azure/gpt-4o` instead of `MODEL=azure/gpt-4o`, it failed, but there is no error information in crewai framework???
Good call. I will work on that soon

